# Candidate F5 (issue 172, near top-down): a gramophone with the horn's mouth toward the player. The front faces north: the brass horn lies along the oak top at the right, its wide mouth with a dark throat at the north end and narrowing back toward the wall; the platter sits at the left. 16x16.
